## Differences and action plan

D1. Decision SB-0102 text is stale against the contract (documentation; the decision is `proposed`, so it can be edited, otherwise supersede). Its "Watch out" says "Two semantic tokens are missing (backdrop color, surface max width)", but Q1 added `color.overlay` and `size.dialog.max-width` and the contract uses both (`dialog.backdrop`, `dialog.max-width`). Action: update the Watch out line (and the `plan.md` token list if it still says "missing"). No code change.

D2. Title text copy is not live (small code gap, within recorded drift). Where element references are unsupported, `#name()` copies `title.textContent` at render time; changing the title text later does not re-render the content, so the dialog name goes stale. Contract.md section 9 says "the title text is copied into the name" without saying it follows later edits; the contract's tests only cover a title added after opening. Action: either accept as a known limitation of the fallback path (add to the "name and description" drift entry) or have the content re-render on title text change (code). Owner decides; low severity, only affects browsers without element references.

D3. `sb-dialog-content` `aria-label` is read through `observedAttributes` and forwarded to the inner dialog, which matches the drift entry, but the host element itself keeps `aria-label` on a `display: contents` wrapper with no role. Axe is clean in the spec (search-palette story), so no action; noted for the owed screen-reader pass.

D4. Items outside the contract, all deliberate and small: (a) Escape is ignored while `isComposing` (IME) and when a control already prevented it (the second is in the contract via Q5, the first is not; add one line to section 9 Keyboard); (b) `aria-haspopup` on the trigger is not set (recorded in drift, with the SB-0009 reason).

D5. `npm run check` fails O1, D1 and a G1 catalog entry (indexes and Command manifest). Action: `sketchbook propagate`, `npm run catalog:build`, and the Figma scripts it lists, before merge. Not a Dialog defect. Dialog's design realization is "Not realized yet" (contract.md Realizations, Figma), which D4 and D3 checks currently accept for a `draft` component.

D6. Owed before beta, not a parity defect: manual VoiceOver (Safari) and NVDA (Chrome, Firefox) pass for the element-reference name and description (Q6, SB-0102); a11y-auditor live keyboard pass; contract status stays `draft` until then.

No behavior divergence between contract and code was found. Every one of the 12 drift entries in `realizations.web.drift` corresponds to observed code, and the contract.md and contract.json Realizations agree.

## Verdict

Matches the contract. The implementation satisfies the props, events, anatomy, states, dimensions, typography, tokens, accessibility and form behavior it defines, with 12 recorded and deliberate drift entries. Open items are documentation or process only: SB-0102's stale "missing tokens" line (D1), one optional wording and one optional code improvement on the title-text fallback (D2, D4a), and the propagate/catalog rebuild before merge (D5). No code fix is required.
